  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile+avgpool is the strongest RNA configuration tested. Image alone is very weak (0.208), so the RNA encoder is the most impactful design axis to explore next. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned latent encoder (scvi_n200) improve accuracy in the same multiprofile+avgpool setup? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002, isolating the effect of the RNA representation. Why: With 5 experiments remaining, establishing the best RNA encoder before moving to multimodal fusion is critical—any multimodal model built on a suboptimal RNA backbone will be limited. If scvi_n200 improves over PCA, we gain a stronger foundation for the remaining experiments; if not, PCA remains our best bet and we can pivot to multimodal testing with confidence."
}

